## Nexus Industries Reports Record FY2025 Results; Issues FY2026 Guidance

### Revenue up 13.9% to $8.45 Billion; EPS up 17.6% to $5.82

**PHOENIX, AZ – January 28, 2026** – Nexus Industries, Inc. (NYSE: NEXS) today announced financial results for its fiscal year ended December 31, 2025.

### FY2025 Highlights

| Metric | FY2025 | FY2024 | Change |
|--------|--------|--------|--------|
| Revenue | $8.45B | $7.42B | +13.9% |
| Operating Income | $945M | $815M | +16.0% |
| Net Income | $755M | $642M | +17.6% |
| Diluted EPS | $5.82 | $4.95 | +17.6% |
| Free Cash Flow | $1.12B | $985M | +13.7% |
| Backlog | $12.4B | $10.8B | +14.8% |

### Q4 2025 Highlights

| Metric | Q4 2025 | Q4 2024 | Change |
|--------|---------|---------|--------|
| Revenue | $2.38B | $2.08B | +14.4% |
| Operating Income | $295M | $241M | +22.4% |
| Diluted EPS | $1.82 | $1.48 | +23.0% |

"FY2025 was a transformational year for Nexus Industries," said Dr. Victoria Chen, CEO. "We achieved record financial performance while advancing strategic programs that position us for long-term growth. Our Falcon X UAV program is on track for first flight, our GreenHydrogen facility is nearing completion, and our partnership with Toyota will revolutionize battery technology."

### Division Performance

**Nexus Aerospace** reported revenue of $2.78 billion, up 12.3% from the prior year, driven by the Falcon X UAV program and strong commercial satellite demand.

**Nexus Energy Systems** achieved revenue of $2.35 billion, up 22.1%, led by the Desert Sun Solar Farm and GreenHydrogen project progress.

**Nexus Digital Solutions** delivered revenue of $2.02 billion, up 18.2%, with NexusConnect IoT and CyberShield security platforms driving growth.

**Nexus Advanced Materials** reported revenue of $1.30 billion, up 8.3%, with strong demand for high-temperature superconducting wire and advanced composites.

### FY2026 Outlook

The Company is providing the following guidance for FY2026:

| Metric | FY2026 Guidance |
|--------|-----------------|
| Revenue | $9.5 - $9.8 billion |
| Operating Margin | 11.5% - 12.0% |
| Diluted EPS | $6.20 - $6.50 |
| Free Cash Flow | $1.2 - $1.3 billion |
| Capital Expenditures | ~$680 million |

"We enter 2026 with strong momentum and a record backlog," said Michael Chang, CFO. "Our diversified portfolio, strong balance sheet, and disciplined capital allocation position us well for continued growth."

### Dividend Increase

The Board of Directors declared a quarterly dividend of $0.45 per share, a 12% increase from the prior year. The dividend is payable on February 28, 2026, to shareholders of record on February 15, 2026.

### Capital Returns

During FY2025, the Company returned $725 million to shareholders through dividends ($440 million) and share repurchases ($285 million). The Board has authorized an additional $500 million for share repurchases.

